[CENTER]
[SIZE=7][B][COLOR=#2C3E50]LeafRTP[/COLOR][COLOR=#2980B9]-Pro[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[SIZE=4][B][COLOR=#555555]High-Performance Random Teleport (RTP) Plugin for Folia, Paper & Spigot[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[/CENTER]

[CENTER][I]Once upon a time, I wanted to explore a minecraft world. I asked for [/I]/rtp[I] in servers I played on. They told me "no, that's laggy", and I took that personally.[/I][/CENTER]

No menu, however polished, can make [I]/rtp[/I] fast - only the engine behind it can. With most random-teleport plugins, [B]any[/B] click can make the server load chunk after chunk after chunk: it picks a spot, loads it on the main thread, and - if it turns out unsafe - tries another, and another, with nothing telling it to stop. That lag spike never shows up in the menu. It shows up in your MSPT, in the stutter every other player feels, and eventually in the players who quietly stop logging in.

[B]LeafRTP-Pro was built on one idea: a teleport should cost the server nothing the player can feel. No spike. No spinner. No quiet churn.[/B]

[B]Enterprise performance, proven not asserted.[/B] 19.8 TP/s sustained at a 4 ms worst-case main-thread tick on Paper (next-best plugin: 70 ms), with audited safety invariants - no unsafe blocks, no force-loaded chunks, no claim-bypassing teleports, no silent failures. Every number on this page is measured on a public harness, not a marketing claim - and bounded worst-case latency is the one axis a Paper-only, on-tick design cannot follow.

[CENTER][I]Supported: Paper, Folia, Spigot, Fabric, and native NeoForge (1.21.x / 26.1.x) - Minecraft 1.20.x / 1.21.x / 26.x. Legacy Forge is not native: run the Spigot/Paper jar under Arclight / Mohist. Works the moment the jar drops in - no tuning required - and rewards operators who like to dig into YAML and profiler output. Drop-in upgrade from the free LeafRTP build.[/I][/CENTER]
[CENTER][COLOR=#A0A0A0]------------------------------------------------------------[/COLOR][/CENTER]

[SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#27AE60]Why operators buy Pro[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[CENTER][SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#27AE60]19.8 TP/s sustained at 4 ms worst-case tick. Next-best plugin: 70 ms.[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE][/CENTER]

[B]If [I]/rtp[/I] is the top entry in your timings report, this is the fix.[/B] LeafRTP-Pro is the polygon-bounded, Folia-native Random Teleport engine for high-load and custom-world Minecraft servers:

[LIST]
[*][B]No lag spikes when players spam [I]/rtp[/I].[/B] Worst-case main-thread tick stays at 4 ms (vs. 70-771 ms for the next plugins) - your TPS holds at 20.00 during a teleport burst.
[*][B]Instant teleports, no "Finding a safe location..." wait.[/B] Pre-verified location queue serves [I]/rtp[/I] in one tick instead of loading chunks on demand.
[*][B]The only LeafRTP plugin that runs natively on Folia without stalling regions.[/B] Per-teleport work stays well under a single region tick; the throughput we measured (9.87 TP/s @ 99.97 % success) was bounded by Region-Scheduler hops in the harness, [I]not[/I] by computation - a floor set by the test rig, not a ceiling on the engine. Every competitor stalls regions or fails to load.
[*][B]Automatic performance the moment the jar drops in.[/B] Pre-warmed location queue, persistent spatial memory, off-tick Anvil pre-filter and async chunk loading kick in on first start - no profiling, no tuning, no per-world hand-holding. Same [I]config.yml[/I], commands, and claim-plugin integrations (GriefDefender, GriefPrevention, Lands, WorldGuard, Towny, Factions, HuskTowns, RedProtect) as the free build, so the upgrade itself is risk-free.
[*][B]Audited safety[/B]: no unsafe blocks, no force-loaded chunks, no claim-bypassing teleports, no silent failures.
[/LIST]

