[I]Methodology: Paper 1.21, 2 OPed clients spamming [I]/rtp[/I] continuously, in-repo harness linked below. Folia and Spigot results in the full benchmark section.[/I]

Same throughput as the next-best plugin at [B]~17x lower worst-case tick spike and 35% less CPU per teleport.[/B] Raw harness: [URL='https://github.com/dailystruggle/RTP/tree/V3/helpers/StressTestRTP'][I]helpers/StressTestRTP/[/I][/URL].

[B]And speed isn't a trade against features.[/B] The same off-tick architecture that holds your TPS also runs the full effects engine, eight bundled claim integrations, multi-server proxy support, SQL/Redis backends, and the [I]safety.yml[/I] token grammar - performance is what makes the feature set affordable, not a compromise against it.

Each capability below is paired with the part of that architecture that makes it cheap to run - the feature set and the performance are the same system, not opposite ends of a dial:

[TABLE]
[TR]
[TH]Feature you get[/TH]
[TH]What makes it cost the server nothing[/TH]
[/TR]
[TR]
[TD][B]Lifecycle effects engine[/B] - multi-phase particles, sounds, titles, fireworks, potions[/TD]
[TD]Effect math and packet work run off the main thread, so they never show up in your MSPT.[/TD]
[/TR]
[TR]
[TD][B]Per-region / per-world controls[/B] - custom shapes, radii, centers, biome filters, safety per region[/TD]
[TD]Locations are pre-warmed and validated in the background queue [I]before[/I] anyone runs [I]/rtp[/I], so depth costs no tick time.[/TD]
[/TR]
[TR]
[TD][B]8 bundled claim integrations[/B] - GriefDefender, GriefPrevention, Lands, WorldGuard, Towny, Factions, HuskTowns, RedProtect[/TD]
[TD]Claim checks reroll inside the async pipeline, not on the tick that teleports the player.[/TD]
[/TR]
[TR]
[TD][B][I]safety.yml[/I] token grammar[/B] - block tags, state predicates, wildcards[/TD]
[TD]The off-tick Anvil ([I].mca[/I]) pre-filter rejects unsafe biomes and oceans by reading region files directly, with no main-thread chunk loads.[/TD]
[/TR]
[TR]
[TD][B]Multi-server proxy + SQL/Redis[/B] - cross-network [I]/rtp[/I], reservation tokens, shared state[/TD]
[TD]State sync runs on async backends; the teleport hot path stays free of foreign-region and blocking API hops.[/TD]
[/TR]
[TR]
[TD][B]Built-in visualizations & observability[/B] - [I]/rtp visualization[/I] region/biome maps and bad-location heatmaps painted onto real map items, MSPT / heap / pipeline-latency sparklines, plus live [I]/rtp info[/I] diagnostics[/TD]
[TD]Charts render from in-memory state through the [I]maps-api[/I] / [I]metrics-api[/I] SPI, so analytics never touch the teleport hot path - no separate heatmap or metrics add-on needed.[/TD]
[/TR]
[TR]
[TD][B]Optional PvP / combat-tag gate[/B] - refuse or delay [I]/rtp[/I] for players who recently dealt or took PvP damage, with native tracking plus PvPManager / CombatLogX / Simple Combat Log integration[/TD]
[TD]Combat state is checked once at [I]/rtp[/I] pre-dispatch through the [I]rtp-api[/I] hook, so the anti-escape rule adds no per-tick cost to the teleport path.[/TD]
[/TR]
[TR]
[TD][B]Developer API[/B] ([I]rtp-api[/I], [I]effects-api[/I]) - pre / mid / post teleport hooks[/TD]
[TD]Hooks fire outside the critical loop, so downstream plugins can't stall your TPS.[/TD]
[/TR]
[/TABLE]

